    "created_at": "2026-11-03T14:35:56Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-03T14:35:56Z",
    "body": "> i didn't follow what the motivation for this cross-origin restriction is, can you clarify more?\n\nI think @smaug---- mentioned this as an idea to make the new cross origin signal allowed, in case it leaks information that we need to contain by default. I'm not sure what a real scenario is where it would be an issue.\n\n> Also, i'm not sure how an event based pattern would work here. there's no trivial JS hook for a page to block its rendering, we intentionally kept it declarative. So its not clear how the embedder would keep its rendering blocked until it gets this event from the embedded document.\n\nI'm not proposing a script exposed DOM event, just a signal from the embedded page to the embedder that it is now render unblocked.",
